{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":3432530,"ns":0,"title":"Cutting tool (machining)","extract":"In the context of machining, a cutting tool or cutter is typically a hardened metal tool that is used to cut, shape, and remove material from a workpiece by means of machining tools as well as abrasive tools by way of shear deformation. The majority of these tools are designed for metals, but are also used on hard rubber, synthetic resins, slate, marble, and other materials.","description":"Hardened tool used to cut material from the workpiece","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}